{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והיה הדם", :translit "vehayah hadam", :gloss "and the blood shall be"} {:he "לכם", :translit "lachem", :gloss "for you"} {:he "לכם", :translit "lachem", :gloss "for you"} {:he "המילה", :translit "hamilah", :gloss "the circumcision"} {:he "מל", :translit "mal", :gloss "circumcised"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "לכם", :b "המילה"} {:kind :other, :note "רמז: circumcision took place that night, linking the blood of the paschal lamb to the blood of circumcision"}], :frame {:text "At the Exodus, Israel required the blood of circumcision as well as the blood of the paschal lamb. Ezekiel 16:6 compares Israel to a newborn girl cast in the field with her navel cord uncut — understood to mean Israel lacked circumcision in Egypt. According to the Mekhilta on Exodus 12:6, the two bloods — circumcision-blood and pesach-blood — were mixed together on that night, fulfilling the verse's dual phrasing.", :sources ["Ezekiel 16:6" "Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael, Pischa 7 on Exodus 12:6"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "לכם", :a-value 90, :b "המילה", :b-value 90, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :other, :note "רמז: circumcision took place that night, linking the blood of the paschal lamb to the blood of circumcision", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:15:07.292436646Z", :model "glm-5.2"}